# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THE LIVE index.html ACTUALLY LOADS FROM vendor/  (updated 2026-08-06)
#
# The page changed. It is no longer the static 2026-07-30 re-skin that pulled
# one stylesheet; it now renders a real cortical mesh with instanced tract
# lines, so it needs FOUR things from vendor/ that used to be excluded:
#
#   vendor/fonts/*.woff2                  six self-hosted faces
#   vendor/three.module.min.js            + vendor/three.core.min.js, which it
#                                         imports internally -- shipping only
#                                         the first gives a hard module error
#   vendor/lines/LineSegments2.js         the tract bundle: one instanced draw
#   vendor/lines/LineSegmentsGeometry.js  call regardless of segment count
#   vendor/lines/LineMaterial.js
#   vendor/mesh/brain-icbm152-v2.bin      663 KB, 39,828 verts (BRN2 format)
#
# Two rules learned the hard way, both still in force:
#
#   1. DO NOT use `vendor/*` + `!vendor/fonts/`. That pattern is correct under
#      git's matcher (verified) but Vercel did NOT honour the directory
#      re-include: deployed 2026-08-05, /vendor/fonts/IBMPlexSans-400.woff2
#      came back 404 and the live site silently fell back to system fonts.
#      Every exclusion below is therefore EXPLICIT, with no negation to get wrong.
#
#   2. vendor/mesh/brain-mni.bin is derived from aces/brainbrowser and is
#      AGPL-3.0. It was served publicly once already (HTTP 200, 2,703,404
#      bytes, 2026-08-05). It is superseded by brain-icbm152.bin and nothing
#      references it. It is excluded BY NAME below -- do not remove that line,
#      and do not switch this file to a directory-level allow that would let it
#      back in. Deleting the file outright is the better fix and is pending.
#
# Keep this list in sync with the page. After ANY deploy, verify against the
# deployed URL, not against git: an ignore pattern that git accepts proves
# nothing about how the host treats it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# AGPL asset -- superseded, must never ship
vendor/mesh/brain-mni.bin

# v1 of the shippable mesh. Superseded 2026-08-06 by brain-icbm152-v2.bin (BRN2:
# same geometry, 836,324 -> 662,624 on disk, 748,625 -> 469,248 on the wire).
# Kept on disk ONLY because scratchpad/pack_mesh_v2.py reads it to build v2 --
# it is the sole surviving source for this mesh, so do not delete it. Excluded
# by name so the two never both ship.
vendor/mesh/brain-icbm152.bin

# Vendored but not used by the live page.
#
# The 2026-08-11 sweep DELETED the rest of what used to be listed here -- the
# bloom/bokeh pipeline, the HDR lighting stack, MarchingCubes, the superseded
# Line2 pair, and lenis -- 2.3 MB of libraries from approaches that had been
# abandoned and, in the case of bloom, explicitly rejected. Their exclusion
# lines went with them: an ignore rule for a file that does not exist is just
# another thing a future session has to work out. See vendor/README.md.
#
# GSAP is kept because it became free at v3.13 and is the recommended way to do
# the DOM choreography this page still hand-rolls. It is excluded until wired.
vendor/gsap.min.js
vendor/ScrollTrigger.min.js
